3. Har task ke liye ek implementation contract
Sabse important naya concept file count nahi, balki har authorized task ke liye implementation se pehle code-to-test traceability hai.

Per-task contract existing evidence folder mein hoga:
REOS_CONTROL_CENTER/evidence/
└── <GATE-ID>/
    └── <TASK-ID>-implementation-contract.json


Example ke liye future APP-001-T08 ka contract REOS_CONTROL_CENTER/evidence/APP-001/APP-001-T08-implementation-contract.json ho sakta hai. Ye example path hai; abhi file create nahi hui hai.

Contract mein ye required fields honge:
Field	Kya prove karna hoga
Authority binding	Live state.json blob SHA, authorized gate/task ID aur baseline commit SHA
File ownership	Har path ka ADD / UPDATE / VERIFY / NO CHANGE / BLOCKED, actual owner aur consumers
Requirements map	Canonical acceptance-criterion IDs se observable behavior tak trace
Interface map	Actual caller, callee, request/response shape, error behavior aur authorization boundary
Test map	Har relevant requirement ke focused, negative/failure aur integration tests
CI execution	Kaunse existing workflow/script tests run karta hai
Release evidence	Actual tested SHA, relevant Actions run, changed-file readback aur unresolved gaps

Ye JSON state.json ka replacement nahi hoga. Task selection aur status canonical state mein hi rahenge; implementation contract us task ka derived work-and-proof record hoga.
4. Generic code ko pakadne wala real gate
Sirf validator banana kaafi nahi. Validator ko existing test pipeline se wire karna aur behavioral proof maangna bhi zaroori hai.
Gate	Pass hone ke liye
Task/scope check	Contract live canonical task aur inspected baseline se match kare
Change-impact check	Changed files aur affected callers/dependencies identify hon
Contract check	Public interfaces, authorization aur failure behavior defined ho
Test-coverage check	Requirements mapped hon; nonexistent ya CI mein invoke na hone wale tests reject hon
Integration check	Cross-boundary code ke liye actual runtime composition test ho
Security check	Unauthorized tenant, invalid input, replay, timeout, quota aur relevant negative cases cover hon
Evidence check	Relevant test result aur source/tree identity independently verifiable ho

Ek important limitation: koi generic JSON validator apne aap prove nahi kar sakta ki test semantically strong hai. Isliye real integration test aur independent diff review mandatory honge. Generic code ko rokne ka actual mechanism yeh combination hai, na ki sirf TODO ya placeholder strings ko scan karna.
5. Existing HOMIO architecture ko kaise use karunga
Main ACRL mein koi naya duplicate implementation engine nahi banaunga. Existing responsibilities ko reuse karke unka actual integration strengthen karunga.
Existing owner	Is process mein role
T16 / T17	Source discovery, dependency analysis aur change-impact
T19	Relevant test selection aur failure diagnosis
T20	Bounded patch verification aur external verification evidence
T21 / T22	Authorized GitHub changes, commit identity aur checkpoint
T23 / T24	Evidence provenance aur cross-chat continuity
T26–T30	Existing loop, dependency scheduling, human decision aur completion/handoff boundaries

In owners ka hona yeh proof nahi ki har end-to-end behavior already wired hai. Jahan integration missing hai, wahan existing contracts aur tests ke through gap close hoga—not by making a second Control Center.
6. AI product par iska application
AI-001 ko dobara open nahi karunga. Lekin live AI integration ke liye ek architecture issue solve karna hoga: approved ARCH-038 Node.js/Fastify backend stack define karta hai, jabki current AI package Python mein hai. Current F08 frontend static preview hai aur live AI API connection nahi hai.

Isliye current runtime boundary ko formal architecture process se resolve kiye bina main guessed API route, second backend ya speculative provider adapter nahi banaunga.

Jab canonical execution workflow AI integration task tak pahunchta hai, tab current existing modules ko ek tested vertical slice mein connect karna hoga:

F08 request → authenticated server boundary → authorized AI platform → existing retrieval → controlled provider call → validated response → usage/observability evidence

Integration tests actual route aur service composition run karenge; sirf end-to-end path ke upar fake handler rakhkar pass nahi karenge. Provider calls test boundary par deterministic ho sakte hain, lekin production wiring verify honi chahiye.
7. Implementation ka order
Main kaam ko is tarah execute karunga:
1. Governance setup: reos-development protection aur reliable PR CI status checks.
2. Contract foundation: schema, validator aur validator ke adversarial tests.
3. Agent consistency: AGENTS.md, targeted EntryPoint rules aur contract regression tests.
4. CI enforcement: existing verification action mein conformance gate integrate karna aur exact failed/pass run verify karna.
5. Product implementation: canonical task ke authorised scope mein real integration, security tests aur release proof.
Tumhare current APP-001-T01 par doosri chat kaam kar rahi hai, isliye main uske live frontend files ko parallel edit nahi karunga. state.json bhi manually change nahi karunga.

Ye structure GitHub Spec Kit ke spec → plan → task → implementation → convergence model aur OpenAI ki coding-agent guidance mein instructions ke saath tests/review rakhne ke approach se align karta hai; main un tools ka poora scaffolding install karke duplicate workflow nahi banaunga. GitHub Spec Kit · OpenAI coding-agent best practices

Mera owner-level decision: pehle branch protection aur implementation-conformance gate ko design karke enforce karna hai. Uske baad har meaningful task actual code, runtime wiring aur required tests ke through prove hoga. Isse generic implementation ko accept karne ka risk kam hoga aur same foundation ko baar-baar redesign karne ki zaroorat bhi kam padegi.

Filhaal ye improved engineering structure aur proposed file matrix hai—maine abhi koi file save ya state.json modify nahi kiya hai.
